  "intro": "Seventh graders determine or clarify the meaning of unknown and multiple-meaning words, using context clues, Greek and Latin roots and affixes, and reference materials (dictionary, glossary, thesaurus). Roots and affixes carry meaning: 'bene' = good, 'mal' = bad, '-logy' = study of.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Use context: 'The benevolent king was loved for his kindness and generosity.'\n\nWhat does 'benevolent' mean?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Context: 'loved for his kindness and generosity.'",
          "The root 'bene' means good.",
          "So 'benevolent' means kind and good-hearted."
        ],
        "answer": "Kind and good-hearted."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "The root 'aqua' means water. What does 'aquatic' mean?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "'aqua' = water, '-ic' relates to.",
          "So 'aquatic' means relating to water."
        ],
        "answer": "Relating to water."
      }
